✅ Success

200 → OK (everything worked)

201 → Created (new resource made, e.g. user registered, post added)

204 → No Content (successful, but nothing to return — e.g. delete)

⚠️ Client Errors

400 → Bad Request (user sent invalid data)

401 → Unauthorized (no or bad token)

403 → Forbidden (valid token, but not allowed — e.g. deleting someone else’s post)

404 → Not Found (user, post, or route doesn’t exist)

409 → Conflict (e.g. duplicate email or username)

422 → Unprocessable Entity (validation failed, like invalid email format)

💥 Server Errors

500 → Internal Server Error (something exploded on your end)

503 → Service Unavailable (database down, maintenance mode)